// | PUMP_RUNTIME_ACC| Accumulates      | Preserved when  | Power-up init to 0 only              | None                | LTIME (ns)       |
// |                 | CycleTime when   | VFD_RUN = FALSE |                                      |                     | 0 to max LTIME   |
// |                 | VFD_RUN = TRUE   |                 |                                      |                     |                  |
// | ViscosityValid  | Valid after      | Retained while  | Immediate on VISCOSITY_OK = FALSE    | None                | Debounced state  |
// |                 | DebounceTime     | VISCOSITY_OK =  | or E-Stop                            |                     |                  |
// |                 |                  | TRUE            |                                      |                     |                  |

// Implementation
The VFD_RUN output activates when the safety permissive is active, viscosity measurements are stable, and the pump isn't already running or flagged for maintenance. The pump command persists as long as these conditions hold, with the E-Stop serving as the highest-priority shutdown signal. PUMP_MAINT_DUE latches once accumulated runtime exceeds 500 hours and remains set as an informational flag. Runtime tracking continues accumulating through each cycle while the pump operates, preserving its value when stopped, and resets only at power-up. Viscosity validation requires the signal to remain steady for the debounce duration before enabling pump operation, clearing immediately if the measurement becomes unstable or an emergency stop occurs. END_IF
